-- lib/linproof.cub — the linear-arithmetic certificate checker, verified (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.13 “F31–F32 — Reflection and certificates”, its part F32).
-- Loaded after lib/std.cub. The checker of lib/lin.cub works over codes; here the same algorithm
-- is defined over a typed fragment and its soundness is a theorem: equal normal forms denote
-- equal words (same-norm-eq), the order check is sound (code-le-sound), and a Farkas certificate
-- that checks proves its goal wherever the hypotheses hold (cert-sound). The subtraction used by
-- the order check is unverified and need not be: the check is an equality test on its result. The elaborator's bridge from a code to the typed fragment is lib/lin.cub's
-- linearize, the same function over codes. Words: plusw is addition by recursion (lib/std.cub),
-- equal to the machine's wadd (plusw≡wadd).
-- Each step of an induction is its own lemma with a signature: the elaborator determines the
-- implicit endpoints of a composed path from a signature, not from a motive applied inside a
-- step function (an item of PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.12 “E28 — Elaboration”).
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- word laws
catw : {x y z : Word} → x ≡ y → y ≡ z → x ≡ z
catw p q = λ i → comp (λ j → Word) (λ j → [ i = 0 ↦ x , i = 1 ↦ q j ]) (p i)
